cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use NovaFabric in your research or tooling, please cite it as below."
title: "NovaFabric: replayable, verifiable execution evidence for AI agents"
abstract: >-
  NovaFabric is self-hosted, open-source replay and evidence infrastructure for
  AI agents and agentic systems. It captures agent executions as portable,
  secret-redacted Run Capsules and provides replay, behavioral and structural
  diff, lineage, cryptographic provenance, assurance, and audit around those
  executions. The same capture layer can wrap general commands and runs in the
  user's own infrastructure, from local environments through Kubernetes to
  SLURM/HPC, with no accounts and no telemetry. It is built around
  five primitives — Asset Registry, Run Capsule, Replay, Lineage, and Evidence
  Bundle — and four replay modes (forensic, mocked, semantic, exact). Evidence
  bundles verify offline with only sha256sum and an ed25519 verifier, requiring
  no NovaFabric installation. Capture works without application code changes and
  interoperates with OpenTelemetry GenAI semantic conventions, in-toto/DSSE,
  RFC 3161, W3C PROV, OpenLineage, and CycloneDX.
